            <ArticleTitle>[Parsonage-Turner syndrome and giant-cell arteritis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>354-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Parsonage-Turner syndrome is an idiopathic brachial neuropathy affecting the 5(th) and the 6(th) roots. Giant-cells arteritis rarely affects the brachial plexus. In such cases, it can mimic Parsonage-Turner syndrome. We report a case focusing on clinical signs suggesting giant-cell arteritis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
